        "title": "Space (video game)",
        "extract": "Space (also called Space I) is a text-based role-playing video game for the Apple II designed  by Steven Pederson and Sherwin Steffin of Edu-Ware Services. It was one of the first science fiction RPGs to appear on personal computers. An expansion pack, Space II by David Mullich, was released in the same year. \nThe game system was based upon the Traveller role-playing-game, created by Game Designers' Workshop, which sued Edu-Ware for copyright infringement in 1982.  In an out-of-court settlement, both Space and Space II were removed from the market.",
